WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:02.202
- Good morning Believe Nation, it's Evan.

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:04.286
My one word is believe, and I believe

00:00:04.286 --> 00:00:06.345
in people more than they
believe in themselves.

00:00:06.345 --> 00:00:09.064
And my sincere hope is
that if you see in yourself

00:00:09.064 --> 00:00:12.290
what I see in you, you'll be
able to change the planet.

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:13.955
So to help you on your journey,

00:00:13.955 --> 00:00:16.403
today's message is "become irreplaceable."

00:00:16.403 --> 00:00:18.660
Over to you, Priyanka Chopra.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:21.377
(rooster crows)

00:00:21.377 --> 00:00:23.406
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:23.406 --> 00:00:26.111
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:00:26.111 --> 00:00:29.611
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:31.077 --> 00:00:32.946
- [Priyanka] When I was
very young, I was 19,

00:00:32.946 --> 00:00:35.126
and I was doing the first
few movies I remember

00:00:35.126 --> 00:00:37.288
the producers would say,
"Well, if she can't work it out

00:00:37.288 --> 00:00:38.939
"it's fine. We'll just cast someone else,

00:00:38.939 --> 00:00:40.440
"girls are replaceable."

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.913
Subconsciously, it
really worked on my mind,

00:00:42.913 --> 00:00:47.444
and I started picking up
parts which were strong,

00:00:47.444 --> 00:00:51.011
which were not just the damsel in distress

00:00:51.011 --> 00:00:52.861
waiting for someone to rescue me.

00:00:52.861 --> 00:00:55.658
Now 13, 15 years later the movies

00:00:55.658 --> 00:00:58.816
that I do, I'm irreplaceable.

00:00:58.816 --> 00:01:00.744
- If you want to be a success
in whatever you're doing

00:01:00.744 --> 00:01:04.355
then you have to be so good at
it that you're irreplaceable.

00:01:04.355 --> 00:01:07.610
If I can swap out your
product or your service

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:10.023
with somebody else's really easily

00:01:10.023 --> 00:01:12.377
then you're never going to stand out,

00:01:12.377 --> 00:01:14.264
you're never going to really
build a successful business.

00:01:14.264 --> 00:01:16.973
It's going to be a race down
to the bottom for price.

00:01:16.973 --> 00:01:18.763
If I can't tell the difference between

00:01:18.763 --> 00:01:22.110
what you're selling and what
your competitors are selling

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:24.659
then I'm just going to go
with whoever is the cheapest.

00:01:24.659 --> 00:01:27.156
And that's where a lot of
entrepreneurs are playing.

00:01:27.156 --> 00:01:28.886
Now price is always going to be important,

00:01:28.886 --> 00:01:31.289
but it's not always the
most important thing

00:01:31.289 --> 00:01:33.619
for a majority of a lot of customers.

00:01:33.619 --> 00:01:36.586
You just haven't done your
job to stand out enough.

00:01:36.586 --> 00:01:38.137
I think it's also really important

00:01:38.137 --> 00:01:40.710
to balance your ego with your humbleness.

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:42.533
I think it's important to have both.

00:01:42.533 --> 00:01:45.448
I think a lot of entrepreneurs
and a lot of people play

00:01:45.448 --> 00:01:48.245
on one side of the spectrum
and not enough of the other.

00:01:48.245 --> 00:01:51.857
And so a lot of entrepreneurs,
we don't have enough ego,

00:01:51.857 --> 00:01:54.138
we don't have enough pride, we
don't have enough confidence

00:01:54.138 --> 00:01:56.497
in ourselves to go out and charge

00:01:56.497 --> 00:01:58.931
what we're worth, to
feel like we're worthy.

00:01:58.931 --> 00:02:01.497
I think a lot of entrepreneurs
could boost their prices

00:02:01.497 --> 00:02:06.445
20, 25, 30% and not see
a dip in their customers.

00:02:06.445 --> 00:02:09.173
I think too many entrepreneurs
just underprice themselves

00:02:09.173 --> 00:02:11.356
because they don't have
enough confidence in what

00:02:11.356 --> 00:02:12.807
they're selling and what they're doing.

00:02:12.807 --> 00:02:15.638
I think too, though, you
balance it with humbleness

00:02:15.638 --> 00:02:19.030
because if you are not humble
then you'll never grow.

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:21.386
And you'll never learn, and
you'll never try to get better,

00:02:21.386 --> 00:02:22.815
and you'll never try to keep improving

00:02:22.815 --> 00:02:24.495
because you think you know everything.

00:02:24.495 --> 00:02:26.227
And so if I look at my
YouTube channel as an example,

00:02:26.227 --> 00:02:28.200
I've had a number of conversations

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:29.756
with different people
talking about my channel,

00:02:29.756 --> 00:02:33.293
and often it'll start with me saying all

00:02:33.293 --> 00:02:34.613
the things that I want to work on.

00:02:34.613 --> 00:02:36.504
Like I need to get better.

00:02:36.504 --> 00:02:38.023
I need to create better content.

00:02:38.023 --> 00:02:41.033
I need to make three solid
videos a day that people love

00:02:41.033 --> 00:02:43.512
and every series is leading
to growth to the channel

00:02:43.512 --> 00:02:46.128
and is having a big impact
on the audience reach.

00:02:46.128 --> 00:02:48.676
And a lot of times the natural reaction

00:02:48.676 --> 00:02:51.024
from people will be to try
to be supportive and say,

00:02:51.024 --> 00:02:53.613
"Well, you're making three videos a day.

00:02:53.613 --> 00:02:57.073
"I'm making one a week," or,
"I struggle to make one a week.

00:02:57.073 --> 00:03:00.528
"You're already doing great.
You're already having such a

00:03:00.528 --> 00:03:02.808
"big impact, you shouldn't
be so hard on yourself."

00:03:02.808 --> 00:03:05.007
And this is where the danger comes in

00:03:05.007 --> 00:03:09.359
because if I just lived
to their expectations,

00:03:09.359 --> 00:03:11.393
You know, I'm just some
big fish in this tiny pond.

00:03:11.393 --> 00:03:13.449
It's easy to feel good
about myself, right?

00:03:13.449 --> 00:03:15.458
It's easy to say, "Well,
you know, you're right."

00:03:15.458 --> 00:03:17.637
If I compare myself to all
these other YouTube channels

00:03:17.637 --> 00:03:20.472
where they're making one video
a week and that's really hard

00:03:20.472 --> 00:03:22.068
and that's really good for them

00:03:22.068 --> 00:03:25.508
then I lower my standards
to where they're at

00:03:25.508 --> 00:03:27.380
and what they see as excellent.

00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:29.922
Or for me, I have greater
standards for myself.

00:03:29.922 --> 00:03:31.987
And so I push myself to want to do more.

00:03:31.987 --> 00:03:33.843
I believe the editing can be better.

00:03:33.843 --> 00:03:35.324
I believe the filming can be better.

00:03:35.324 --> 00:03:36.675
I believe I can be better.

00:03:36.675 --> 00:03:38.236
I believe the content
we have can be better.

00:03:38.236 --> 00:03:39.633
Everything can always be better

00:03:39.633 --> 00:03:41.395
and that'll push ourselves
to go out and do it.

00:03:41.395 --> 00:03:44.312
And at the same time, I think my channel

00:03:44.312 --> 00:03:46.406
is the greatest YouTube channel, period.

00:03:46.406 --> 00:03:48.984
I think my channel is a gift to humanity.

00:03:48.984 --> 00:03:51.642
I think if a YouTube
channel was going to win

00:03:51.642 --> 00:03:54.293
a Nobel prize it should be my channel.

00:03:54.293 --> 00:03:56.645
I love my channel, I
consume my own channel more

00:03:56.645 --> 00:03:59.830
than any other channel and I
think it's a gift to humanity,

00:03:59.830 --> 00:04:03.429
I do, I believe that, and it
needs to get a lot better.

00:04:03.429 --> 00:04:05.101
Right, so embracing both sides.

00:04:05.101 --> 00:04:08.356
And so I think feeling that
same way about your business,

00:04:08.356 --> 00:04:10.686
feeling like the work that you're doing

00:04:10.686 --> 00:04:13.167
can always get better, can always improve.

00:04:13.167 --> 00:04:15.307
You can improve your
skills and your hustle,

00:04:15.307 --> 00:04:17.550
and your drive, and how
much practice you put in it,

00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:19.632
and energy, and there's
always something new to learn.

00:04:19.632 --> 00:04:21.111
You're never done learning, as soon

00:04:21.111 --> 00:04:22.546
as you stop learning you're done.

00:04:22.546 --> 00:04:24.424
And you're also providing a lot of value.

00:04:24.424 --> 00:04:27.100
You have a great product
or a great service.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.713
There's a lot of love that goes in.

00:04:28.713 --> 00:04:30.469
There's a noticeable
difference between you

00:04:30.469 --> 00:04:32.856
and somebody else, the
rest of your competition.

00:04:32.856 --> 00:04:35.791
Feeling that because
if you don't feel that,

00:04:35.791 --> 00:04:37.292
you're customers won't feel that either.

00:04:37.292 --> 00:04:39.849
If somebody gets on the call
with you or meets with you

00:04:39.849 --> 00:04:43.255
and you can't, with pride,
explain why you're different

00:04:43.255 --> 00:04:45.532
and why you're better, and
for them to see that result.

00:04:45.532 --> 00:04:48.406
If they can't see it they're
not going to pay you more,

00:04:48.406 --> 00:04:50.569
they're not going to pick
you over somebody else.

00:04:50.569 --> 00:04:52.303
And that means, ultimately, you can't grow

00:04:52.303 --> 00:04:54.212
your business as big as it should be.

00:04:54.212 --> 00:04:56.806
It's the balance, humbleness plus

00:04:56.806 --> 00:05:00.723
ego/confidence become irreplaceable.

00:05:01.775 --> 00:05:03.597
So the question of the
day today is, I'm curious,

00:05:03.597 --> 00:05:05.670
what is the thing that
makes you irreplaceable?

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:07.612
What's so special, unique, different

00:05:07.612 --> 00:05:10.478
about your business that nobody
else can do just like you.

00:05:10.478 --> 00:05:12.587
Leave it down in the comments below,

00:05:12.587 --> 00:05:14.016
I'm really curious to find out.

00:05:14.016 --> 00:05:15.289
And also if you leave a comment

00:05:15.289 --> 00:05:16.929
within the first couple hours
of this video going live

00:05:16.929 --> 00:05:19.762
you have a chance of winning
one of our two daily prizes.

00:05:19.762 --> 00:05:22.357
I also want to give a quick
shout-out to Dev Gadhvi.

00:05:22.357 --> 00:05:24.370
Dev, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book

00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:26.778
and doing a review on your
channel for your audience.

00:05:26.778 --> 00:05:29.154
CareNation, for doing
the interview with Lily,

00:05:29.154 --> 00:05:31.519
and all the love and support you've given

00:05:31.519 --> 00:05:33.065
for my book, "Your One Word."

00:05:33.065 --> 00:05:34.681
I really appreciate it man and I'm so glad

00:05:34.681 --> 00:05:36.192
that you enjoyed the read.

00:05:36.192 --> 00:05:37.580
Thank you guys again for watching.

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:39.309
I believe in you, I hope you continue

00:05:39.309 --> 00:05:42.081
to believe in yourself, and
whatever your one word is.

00:05:42.081 --> 00:05:44.884
Much love and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:05:44.884 --> 00:05:47.575
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:05:47.575 --> 00:05:49.868
♫ I wake up every morning

00:05:49.868 --> 00:05:53.451
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:05:56.712 --> 00:06:00.942
- You know, in your life
you will start a job

00:06:00.942 --> 00:06:03.689
and this is what I say that
every single new person coming

00:06:03.689 --> 00:06:06.940
into Pixar, no matter what you do

00:06:06.940 --> 00:06:10.892
make yourself indispensable
to that organization.

00:06:10.892 --> 00:06:14.009
Make yourself indispensable.

00:06:14.009 --> 00:06:16.351
Where people, after
you're done with your job

00:06:16.351 --> 00:06:19.918
people cannot imagine
the place without you.

00:06:19.918 --> 00:06:24.696
And without asking for a
thing your career will be set.

00:06:24.696 --> 00:06:28.437
- You can be a history
maker or you can be liked

00:06:28.437 --> 00:06:31.378
by everyone around you, you can't be both.

00:06:31.378 --> 00:06:35.622
I mean the very nature of
living your personal greatness

00:06:35.622 --> 00:06:39.726
and doing something
otherworldly in our world

00:06:39.726 --> 00:06:42.015
of ours means you're going to have

00:06:42.015 --> 00:06:44.004
to think differently from the majority.

00:06:44.004 --> 00:06:46.002
You're going to have to install the habits

00:06:46.002 --> 00:06:49.298
and routines that most people don't do.

00:06:49.298 --> 00:06:53.465
You're going to have to live,
talk, breathe, walk, work,

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:58.400
produce, create in a way that most people

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:01.252
who are card carrying members of the cult

00:07:01.252 --> 00:07:04.277
of mediocrity just don't buy into.

00:07:04.277 --> 00:07:07.041
I mean you look at most
people out on the world today,

00:07:07.041 --> 00:07:10.065
and this is not judging,
this is just reporting,

00:07:10.065 --> 00:07:13.049
but they're addicted to
entertainment, they love gossiping.

00:07:13.049 --> 00:07:14.803
They're negative. They're toxic.

00:07:14.803 --> 00:07:16.519
Anyone who wants to do anything great,

00:07:16.519 --> 00:07:18.244
they want to bring them down.

00:07:18.244 --> 00:07:20.697
They dismiss the game changers

00:07:20.697 --> 00:07:22.779
and they're just coasting through life.

00:07:22.779 --> 00:07:26.187
And so the very nature of
you stepping up your game,

00:07:26.187 --> 00:07:30.354
living your greatest
potential, owning your craft,

00:07:31.309 --> 00:07:35.218
dominating your field, and
living a life that's legendary

00:07:35.218 --> 00:07:37.430
means you're going to have to leave the 5%

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:41.670
and make a decision to
live as very few people do.

00:07:41.670 --> 00:07:43.078
And what does that mean?

00:07:43.078 --> 00:07:44.732
It means you're going to be laughed at.

00:07:44.732 --> 00:07:46.322
It means you're going to be ridiculed.

00:07:46.322 --> 00:07:49.074
It means you're going to be misunderstood

00:07:49.074 --> 00:07:51.301
because leadership is a lonely sport.

00:07:51.301 --> 00:07:53.566
And it means you just might be hated.

00:07:53.566 --> 00:07:56.671
- We talk about coolers,
we talk about closers,

00:07:56.671 --> 00:07:58.380
and we talk about cleaners.

00:07:58.380 --> 00:07:59.695
Cleaners are going to get you

00:07:59.695 --> 00:08:01.647
that end result over and over again.

00:08:01.647 --> 00:08:05.450
They are so well prepared
and their instincts are

00:08:05.450 --> 00:08:09.213
so sharp they already know what to do.

00:08:09.213 --> 00:08:12.965
If there's a person that's
producing exceptionally,

00:08:12.965 --> 00:08:14.807
there's a reason behind it.

00:08:14.807 --> 00:08:18.974
It's the process, the constant
challenge to get there again,

00:08:20.069 --> 00:08:24.236
and again, and again is what
drives these individuals.

00:08:25.523 --> 00:08:28.038
Everyone talks about "We
want to be legendary."

00:08:28.038 --> 00:08:32.038
You want to be iconic,
don't settle for legendary.

